# Escape Tunnel's "target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn" is an effect of a resolved ability on
# the creature, not an ability it gains (CR 113.1a: abilities are granted with "has" or "gains"; CR 611.2c). Bot2's Turn to
# Frog, cast after it resolved, takes every ability Llanowar Elves has (CR 613.1f) - its "{T}: Add {G}" is gone - but not
# the restriction on blocking it (CR 509.1b): Bot2's Ornithopter may not block the 1/1 blue Frog (the refusal), and Bot2
# takes 1. On turn 5, the turn over, the same attack can be blocked (the positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Escape Tunnel
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Turn to Frog
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Escape Tunnel.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Escape Tunnel.Activate(Ability: can't be blocked; Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Turn to Frog.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Subtypes = Frog
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
! Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.CantBeBlocked = true
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.CantBeBlocked = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Graveyard = Escape Tunnel
Bot2.Graveyard = Turn to Frog
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Subtypes = Druid; Elf
